<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Han Tuozhou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1152–1207</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Han Tuozhou was a chief minister of the Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a>, related by marriage to the imperial family, who dominated the court from the 1190s. He banned the teachings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhu-xi">Zhu Xi</a> as 'false learning' and in 1206 launched a war to recover northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from the Jin. The offensive failed, and in 1207 he was murdered by court rivals, who sent his head to the Jin under the peace of 1208.</p></div>
